        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58849388?u=08f6cc6d91f53b66e6fce613311b6868aa6f16cf&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a focused section to the WebExtensions <code class=\"notranslate\">background</code> manifest documentation explaining how a Manifest V3 extension can specify both <code class=\"notranslate\">background.scripts</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">background.service_worker</code> for cross-browser background behavior.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The update also clarifies that <code class=\"notranslate\">background.preferred_environment</code> is not required for the basic fallback behavior, and should only be used when an extension specifically wants to prefer a service worker where available.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44100.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4433445950\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44100\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44100/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44100\">#44100</a>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Validation</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npx --yes prettier@3.8.3 --check \"files/en-us/mozilla/add-ons/webextensions/manifest.json/background/index.md\"</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">npx --yes --package markdownlint-cli2@0.22.1 --package markdownlint-rule-search-replace@1.2.0 markdownlint-cli2 \"files/en-us/mozilla/add-ons/webextensions/manifest.json/background/index.md\"</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">git diff --check</code></li>\n</ul>",
