        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Replaces a link to the <code class=\"notranslate\">contextMenus</code> API, with a link to the <code class=\"notranslate\">menus</code> API.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Resolves the only remaining <code class=\"notranslate\">webextapiref</code> flaw.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See: <a href=\"https://caugner.github.io/mdn-flawless/#locale=en-US&amp;templ=webextapiref\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://caugner.github.io/mdn-flawless/#locale=en-US&amp;templ=webextapiref</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4231421689\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1462\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/fred/issues/1462/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1462\">mdn/fred#1462</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Follow-up of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4401756693\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44041\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/44041/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44041\">#44041</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44090",
            "title": "Replace another `webextapiref` link for `contextMenus`",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-12T23:29:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-12T11:28:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122352170?u=091ab980244274ed0342cf177e339f5c829027d7&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add a new <code class=\"notranslate\">aria-*</code> row to the HTML attributes table. The attribute name link points to <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Reference/Attributes\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Reference/Attributes</a>. This family of attributes is a bit of an outlier regarding the <code class=\"notranslate\">Element</code> column because members don't all apply to the same set of elements, hence the phrasing \"Depends on the specific attribute\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also struggled to find a good page to link to in the description. <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Accessibility/WAI-ARIA_basics\" rel=\"nofollow\">Understanding ARIA Basics</a> looked good but it is a learn page and not a reference so it might not be exactly what users are looking for. In the end I went for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Guides\" rel=\"nofollow\">ARIA Guides</a> even though it's not only related to ARIA attributes.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">ARIA attributes are HTML attributes so they need to be mentioned in the HTML attributes table.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #44079.\">Closes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4423627624\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44079\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44079/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44079\">#44079</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44086",
            "title": "Add aria-* to HTML attributes index table",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-13T09:23:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-12T08:35:33.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "TGianella",
                "url": "https://github.com/TGianella"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This adds a new guide in \"Defenses\" on \"operational security\", which I've defined basically as processes around developing, building, shipping, and updating software.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It overlaps considerably with supply chain security, and most of its content is taken from the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Attacks/Supply_chain_attacks\" rel=\"nofollow\">Supply chain attacks</a> article. It's not a complete overlap though, in particular we talk about logging and monitoring in this guide, and we talk about SRI in supply chain security but not in this guide.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44065",
            "title": "Operational security guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-13T07:43:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-10T20:04:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wbamberg",
                "url": "https://github.com/wbamberg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54764038?u=07466b64651e022915fbbaf062d487e0b7c9d098&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Document the <code class=\"notranslate\">address</code> option for <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Memory()</code>, including the <code class=\"notranslate\">\"i32\"</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">\"i64\"</code> address types. This also clarifies the BigInt requirements for <code class=\"notranslate\">\"i64\"</code> memories and updates <code class=\"notranslate\">Memory.prototype.grow()</code> to describe its BigInt behavior for <code class=\"notranslate\">\"i64\"</code> memories.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">address</code> option is currently missing from the MDN documentation for <code class=\"notranslate\">WebAssembly.Memory()</code>. Adding it helps readers understand how to create Memory64 memories from JavaScript and avoid using Number values where BigInt values are required.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is defined in the WebAssembly JavaScript Interface:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">AddressType</code> is defined as <code class=\"notranslate\">\"i32\"</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">\"i64\"</code>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">MemoryDescriptor</code> includes an <code class=\"notranslate\">address</code> member.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">Memory(descriptor)</code> constructor defaults <code class=\"notranslate\">address</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">\"i32\"</code> when omitted, and converts <code class=\"notranslate\">initial</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">maximum</code> using the selected address type.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">grow(delta)</code> also converts <code class=\"notranslate\">delta</code> using the memory's address type and returns the previous size using the same address type.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Spec references:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-js-api-2/#enumdef-addresstype\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-js-api-2/#enumdef-addresstype</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-js-api-2/#dom-memorydescriptor-address\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-js-api-2/#dom-memorydescriptor-address</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-js-api-2/#dom-memory-memory\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-js-api-2/#dom-memory-memory</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-js-api-2/#dom-memory-grow\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.w3.org/TR/wasm-js-api-2/#dom-memory-grow</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43904.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4310073497\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43904\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43904/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43904\">#43904</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44051",
            "title": "docs(wasm): add document Memory address option",
